cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SCOBY Watch in research, education, or software development,
  please cite this software using the metadata below.
title: >-
  SCOBY Watch: A Simulation-First IoT and Hybrid Decision Support Framework
  for Kombucha Fermentation Readiness Assessment
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Soma
    given-names: Panji Arya
  - family-names: Nasrulloh
    given-names: Anas
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  SCOBY Watch is a simulation-first Internet of Things and hybrid
  decision-support research prototype for kombucha fermentation readiness
  assessment. It integrates synthetic fermentation data generation, a
  deterministic rule engine, a supervised machine-learning baseline,
  confidence-aware hybrid arbitration, a Flask inference API, MQTT,
  Node-RED, Wokwi simulation, dashboard visualization, automated tests, and
  reproducibility-oriented documentation. The project validates software
  architecture and integration behavior before empirical fermentation data
  and calibrated physical sensors are available.
keywords:
  - kombucha
  - fermentation
  - internet of things
  - IoT
  - machine learning
  - decision support
  - hybrid decision system
  - synthetic data
  - ESP32
  - MQTT
  - Node-RED
  - Wokwi
